; battle.asong: a fight song that follows the fight. The .song text, plus sections (each a
; set of order lists the voices take at their next pattern's end) and states (a section and
; each voice's layer, in steps down). Played by tools/music/adaptive/adaptive.py with a player
; that has two small additions (README.md there: what they cost).
;
; Key: D minor (D major when the fight is nearly won). Tempo: an 8th is 12 ticks (quarter =
; 150 bpm), a bar 96 ticks (1.6 s). Every pattern of the harmony's voices (lead, counter, bass)
; is 2 bars (192 ticks), so every voice reaches a pattern's end on the same tick and a section
; change lands on the next 2-bar line, 3.2 s at most after the game asks; the drums' patterns
; are a bar, so they may change a bar sooner, which reads as a lead-in.
;
; Sections (the order lists; "start" is the song's header):
;   start, main  Dm Bb | C A, 8 bars. The Catwiz motif (D A G# A F | E D), sequenced on C
;                (C G F# G E), the twitch home on A (E D# E C# A); the 2nd time the motif on C
;                leaps an octave and the bar falls to C#, into D again
;   danger       the cat low: Dm pedal, half time. The bass a heartbeat (D D ... C# C#), the
;                lead only the twitch (G# A) and a nervous turn, the counter creeping A Bb A G#
;   king         an elite winding up: the King's motif (the cat's upside down, D G G# G Bb |
;                C D) in the bass and doubled two octaves up on the counter, the drums
;                pounding quarters, the lead's twitch as an alarm over it
;   victory      the enemy nearly beaten: the motif turns major over the same bass and drums
;                (D A G# A F#), climbs (F G A Bb), and ends each phrase on a high C# that
;                pulls into the next
; States (the game picks one; the section and each voice's layer, 0 full .. 15 silent):
;   calm      the player thinking: main, the drums and hats out, the lead and bass softer
;   fight     main, everything but the counter
;   low       the enemy low: main with the counter in and the hats up: fuller
;   danger    the cat low: the danger section, hats out
;   windup    the elite winding up: the king section, all in
;   victory   the victory section, all in
;
; Left (chip 1): the lead, the counter, the hats. Right (chip 2): the bass, the drums, the
;   lead's echo. Voice 2 (hats) is lent to the hero's effects, voice 5 (the echo) to the
;   enemies': the least missed parts.
; voice 0  the lead (v12, the default; its patterns set no volume, so voice 5 shares them)
; voice 1  the counter: two chord tones a bar; the King's motif in king
; voice 2  hats, 8ths (noise on the left chip, alone there)
; voice 3  bass: root, root, octave (3+3+2); the heartbeat in danger; the King's motif in king
; voice 4  drums: kick and snare (noise on the right chip, alone there)
; voice 5  the lead's echo, a dotted 8th (18 ticks) late and soft
(pattern m1 "k3 l12 d5 l36 a5 l12 g#5 a5 l24 f5 l12 e5 l36 d5 l24 r l12 f5 g5")
(pattern m2 "l12 c5 l36 g5 l12 f#5 g5 l24 e5 l12 e5 d#5 l24 e5 c#5 a4")
(pattern m3 "l12 c5 l36 c6 l12 b5 c6 l24 g5 l12 a5 g5 l24 e5 l48 c#5")
(pattern c1 "v9 k6 l48 f4 a4 d4 f4")
(pattern c2 "e4 g4 c#4 e4")
(pattern hats "m2 n1 v7 k1 l12 c4 v4 c4")
(pattern b1 "v12 k4 l36 d2 d2 l24 d3 l36 a#1 a#1 l24 a#2")
(pattern b2 "l36 c2 c2 l24 c3 l36 a1 a1 l24 a2")
(pattern groove "k1 v12 m1 l24 g1 m2 n5 c4 m1 l12 g1 g1 m2 l24 c4")
(pattern in_echo "v5 l18 r")
(pattern d1 "k3 l12 g#4 a4 l36 r r l12 g#4 a4 c5 a4 l48 r")
(pattern db "v12 k2 l12 d2 d2 l36 r r l12 c#2 c#2 l36 r r")
(pattern half "k1 v12 m1 l48 g1 m2 n5 c4")
(pattern kc "v13 k4 l12 d4 l36 g3 l12 g#3 g3 l24 a#3 l12 c4 l36 d4 l48 r")
(pattern kb "v12 k4 l12 d2 l36 g1 l12 g#1 g1 l24 a#1 l12 c2 l36 d2 l12 d1 d1 d1 d1")
(pattern pound "k1 v12 m1 l24 g1 g1 g1 m2 n5 c4")
(pattern v1 "k3 l12 d5 l36 a5 l12 g#5 a5 l24 f#5 l12 e5 l36 d5 l12 a#4 c5 d5 e5")
(voice 0 m1 m2 m1 m3)
(voice 1 c1 c2)
(voice 2 hats)
(voice 3 b1 b2)
(voice 4 groove)
(voice 5 in_echo loop m1 m2 m1 m3)
(section main
    (voice 0 m1 m2 m1 m3)
    (voice 1 c1 c2)
    (voice 3 b1 b2)
    (voice 4 groove)
    (voice 5 m1 m2 m1 m3))
(section danger
    (voice 0 d1)
    (voice 3 db)
    (voice 4 half)
    (voice 5 d1))
(section king
    (voice 1 kc)
    (voice 3 kb)
    (voice 4 pound))
(section victory
    (voice 0 v1 m3)
    (voice 3 b1 b2)
    (voice 4 groove)
    (voice 5 v1 m3))
;      name     section  layers: voice 0  1  2  3  4  5
(state calm     main              3 15 15  3 15  2)
(state fight    main              0 15 15  0  0  0)
(state low      main              0  0  0  0  0  0)
(state danger   danger            0 15 15  0  0  0)
(state windup   king             15  0  0  0  0 15)
(state victory  victory           0 15  0  0  0  0)
